window.ENGLISH_NEWS={"panelTitle":"新闻英语","recommendedOn":"2026-10-10","verifiedAt":"2026-10-10T09:21:00Z","timeZone":"Asia/Shanghai","displayNote":"基于来源报道事实编写的学习改写；非原文转载，非实时更新。","articles":[{"id":"unesco-mexico-school-screens-20261009","title":"UNESCO calls for pairing school screen regulation in Mexico with digital literacy and continuous monitoring","titleZh":"教科文组织呼吁墨西哥将校园屏幕管理与数字素养教育相结合","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-calls-pairing-school-screen-regulation-mexico-digital-literacy-and-continuous-monitoring","publishedAt":"2026-10-09","topic":"文化与教育","learningReason":"围绕校园手机话题学习提出建议和比较政策的英文表达。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"9 October 2026","paragraphs":["UNESCO has called for Mexico's rules on school screens to be supported by stronger digital education. Speaking at an education forum, its representative welcomed an agreement to regulate mobile devices in schools. He also argued that schools need to consider when technology can support inclusion.","Digital tools can help learners who face barriers to attending classes or accessing suitable materials. However, students and communities also need to understand how online platforms work. UNESCO highlighted the importance of skills for judging information and recognising the effects of digital systems.","The organisation also encouraged schools to record and review their experiences. Restricting phones alone cannot solve every learning problem. Reading, writing, reasoning and memory remain important. So do play and working with others. The discussion therefore connected screen rules with a broader question: how can technology serve the goals of education?"],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"regulate","phonetic":"","meaning":"规范管理"},{"word":"inclusion","phonetic":"","meaning":"教育包容性"},{"word":"platforms","phonetic":"","meaning":"网络平台"},{"word":"reasoning","phonetic":"","meaning":"推理能力"}],"questions":[{"options":["Digital education","Phone restrictions alone","Less review of classroom experience","Rules set only by online platforms"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第一段明确说校园屏幕规定需要更强的数字教育支持；第三段还要求记录和回顾经验，因此仅靠限制手机不够。","prompt":"What supports screen rules?","evidence":"UNESCO has called for Mexico's rules on school screens to be supported by stronger digital education."},{"options":["Screen restrictions alone","Technology without monitoring","Replacing classroom cooperation","Reading and reasoning"],"answer":3,"explanation":"第三段列出阅读、写作、推理、记忆、游戏和合作，说明这些能力仍然重要；文中没有说应由屏幕规定取代它们。","prompt":"What remains important?","evidence":"Reading, writing, reasoning and memory remain important."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-calls-pairing-school-screen-regulation-mexico-digital-literacy-and-continuous-monitoring","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"He also argued that schools need to consider when technology can support inclusion.","translation":"他还提出，学校需要考虑技术在什么情况下能够促进教育包容。","analysis":"argued 后接 that 宾语从句；when 引导的从句作 consider 的宾语，使用陈述语序。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":139,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"UNESCO has called for Mexico's rules on school screens to be supported by stronger digital education. Speaking at an education forum, its representative welcomed an agreement to regulate mobile devices in schools. He also argued that schools need to consider when technology can support inclusion."},{"id":"unesco-girls-education-prize-20261009","title":"UNESCO awards 2026 Prize for Girls’ and Women’s Education to transformative projects in Morocco and Peru","titleZh":"摩洛哥和秘鲁项目获2026年教科文组织女童和妇女教育奖","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-awards-2026-prize-girls-and-womens-education-transformative-projects-morocco-and-peru","publishedAt":"2026-10-09","topic":"文化与教育","learningReason":"通过教育项目报道积累平等机会、奖项与社区行动相关表达。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"9 October 2026","paragraphs":["Two education projects have won UNESCO's 2026 prize for girls and women. One works in Morocco, while the other is run by CARE Peru. The winners received their awards in Paris on October 9. Each project received money to continue its work.","In Morocco, Project Soar helps girls stay in school and prepare for their futures. Local women lead activities that build confidence and knowledge about health and rights. The project also brings parents, teachers and other community members into discussions about challenges facing girls.","CARE Peru supports girls in rural and Indigenous communities. Its work combines classroom learning with practical preparation for further education and employment. The programme includes mentoring and financial education. Both projects show that helping girls finish school can involve action beyond the classroom. Families, local leaders and schools all have roles to play."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"awards","phonetic":"","meaning":"奖项"},{"word":"confidence","phonetic":"","meaning":"信心"},{"word":"mentoring","phonetic":"","meaning":"导师指导"},{"word":"employment","phonetic":"","meaning":"就业"}],"questions":[{"options":["Morocco and Peru","Japan and France","Canada and India","Egypt and Spain"],"answer":0,"explanation":"两个获奖项目分别来自摩洛哥和秘鲁。","prompt":"Where are the winning projects?","evidence":"One works in Morocco, while the other is run by CARE Peru."},{"options":["Schools acting without community involvement","Families and communities","Only the award organisers in Paris","Only the students themselves"],"answer":1,"explanation":"末段说明家庭、当地领导者和学校都可参与，支持女童完成学业不限于课堂内。","prompt":"Who helps beyond schools?","evidence":"Both projects show that helping girls finish school can involve action beyond the classroom. Families, local leaders and schools all have roles to play."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-awards-2026-prize-girls-and-womens-education-transformative-projects-morocco-and-peru","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Both projects show that helping girls finish school can involve action beyond the classroom.","translation":"这两个项目都表明，帮助女童完成学业可能需要课堂以外的行动。","analysis":"show 后接 that 引导的宾语从句；helping girls finish school 是动名词短语，在从句中作主语。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":138,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Two education projects have won UNESCO's 2026 prize for girls and women. One works in Morocco, while the other is run by CARE Peru. The winners received their awards in Paris on October 9. Each project received money to continue its work."},{"id":"unesco-burundi-assessment-20261009","title":"Burundi adopts a national strategy to use assessment as a tool for improving learning outcomes","titleZh":"布隆迪通过国家战略，以评估改善学习成效","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/burundi-adopts-national-strategy-use-assessment-tool-improving-learning-outcomes","publishedAt":"2026-10-09","topic":"文化与教育","learningReason":"适合练习辨认教育政策新闻中的目标、措施与结果。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"9 October 2026","paragraphs":["Burundi has adopted a national strategy that aims to make school assessment more useful. The education ministry worked with UNESCO on the plan. A workshop in Bujumbura brought participants together to review the strategy and its practical action plan in September.","Tests can show how well students perform, but the new approach goes further. Officials want learning data to help guide decisions about education. Information about student results can be compared with information about the resources available in schools. This can help identify where extra support is needed.","Participants discussed the strategy's priorities and whether its action plan could be carried out with available institutions, skills and funding. The wider goal is to strengthen the education system. Assessment would then serve as a tool for improvement, rather than simply a way to measure and rank students' performance."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"assessment","phonetic":"","meaning":"学习评估"},{"word":"resources","phonetic":"","meaning":"学校可用资源"},{"word":"funding","phonetic":"","meaning":"资金支持"},{"word":"rank","phonetic":"","meaning":"按表现排名"}],"questions":[{"options":["Student rankings alone","School decisions without learning data","Education decisions","Funding plans that ignore student needs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二段说明学习数据应帮助教育决策并识别额外支持需求；末段强调不只是排名。","prompt":"What should assessment guide?","evidence":"Officials want learning data to help guide decisions about education."},{"options":["Results and resources","Test scores and student rankings only","Funding and travel costs only","Workshop attendance and school holidays"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段明确将学生成绩信息与学校资源信息比较，目的是识别哪里需要更多支持。","prompt":"Which information is compared?","evidence":"Information about student results can be compared with information about the resources available in schools."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/burundi-adopts-national-strategy-use-assessment-tool-improving-learning-outcomes","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Information about student results can be compared with information about the resources available in schools.","translation":"学生成绩信息可以与学校可用资源的信息进行比较。","analysis":"can be compared 是情态动词加被动语态；available in schools 后置修饰 resources。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":137,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Burundi has adopted a national strategy that aims to make school assessment more useful. The education ministry worked with UNESCO on the plan. A workshop in Bujumbura brought participants together to review the strategy and its practical action plan in September."},{"id":"unesco-teacher-prize-20261008","title":"Innovative teacher development initiatives from Ethiopia, Indonesia and Türkiye win the 2026 UNESCO-Hamdan Prize","titleZh":"埃塞俄比亚、印度尼西亚和土耳其教师发展项目获2026年教科文组织哈姆丹奖","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/innovative-teacher-development-initiatives-ethiopia-indonesia-and-turkiye-win-2026-unesco-hamdan","publishedAt":"2026-10-08","topic":"文化与教育","learningReason":"借助三个国家的案例练习比较阅读并积累教师培训词汇。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"8 October 2026","paragraphs":["Education organisations in Ethiopia, Indonesia and Türkiye have won the 2026 UNESCO-Hamdan Prize. Their projects take different approaches to helping teachers develop. Together, they illustrate how stronger support for teachers can improve learning and benefit wider communities.","In Ethiopia, a teacher education college works with local craftspeople to produce classroom learning materials. The materials use local resources and support early childhood education. Future teachers also learn how to create and use these tools. In Indonesia, a foundation helps teachers develop leadership skills through professional communities and cooperation with local partners.","The Turkish winner offers a free festival where teachers lead workshops and learn from colleagues. Sessions cover topics including inclusive education and teacher well-being. The three examples share an important idea: professional learning can grow through practical experience and exchange. Teachers are active contributors to educational change, as well as learners themselves."],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"craftspeople","phonetic":"","meaning":"手工艺人"},{"word":"leadership","phonetic":"","meaning":"领导能力"},{"word":"colleagues","phonetic":"","meaning":"同事"},{"word":"inclusive","phonetic":"","meaning":"包容性的"}],"questions":[{"options":["Teachers working without local partners","Teachers and craftspeople","Only visiting festival speakers","Only the Indonesian foundation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第二段说明埃塞俄比亚师范学院与当地手工艺人合作制作教具；未来教师也学习制作和使用。","prompt":"Who makes Ethiopian materials?","evidence":"In Ethiopia, a teacher education college works with local craftspeople to produce classroom learning materials."},{"options":["Workshops led only by foreign visitors","Competitions to sell classroom materials","Teacher workshops","Examinations that replace peer learning"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第三段说明教师在免费节庆中主持工作坊并向同行学习，不是由考试取代同伴交流。","prompt":"What happens at the festival?","evidence":"The Turkish winner offers a free festival where teachers lead workshops and learn from colleagues."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/innovative-teacher-development-initiatives-ethiopia-indonesia-and-turkiye-win-2026-unesco-hamdan","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Together, they illustrate how stronger support for teachers can improve learning and benefit wider communities.","translation":"这些项目共同说明，加强对教师的支持如何能够改善学习并惠及更广泛的社区。","analysis":"how 引导宾语从句；improve 与 benefit 是由 and 连接、共同受 can 支配的并列动词。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":142,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Education organisations in Ethiopia, Indonesia and Türkiye have won the 2026 UNESCO-Hamdan Prize. Their projects take different approaches to helping teachers develop. Together, they illustrate how stronger support for teachers can improve learning and benefit wider communities."},{"id":"nasa-webb-fast-radio-burst-20261008","title":"Webb Measures Distance to Farthest Fast Radio Burst, Suggesting Origin","titleZh":"韦布测定最遥远快速射电暴的距离，探寻其起源","source":"NASA Science","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/webb-measures-distance-to-farthest-fast-radio-burst-suggesting-origin/","publishedAt":"2026-10-08","topic":"科学与科技","learningReason":"适合练习区分科学观察、研究推测与证据强弱的英语表达。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 08, 2026","paragraphs":["A brief radio signal has given astronomers a new way to investigate the early universe. Using the Webb telescope, researchers identified the galaxy behind the most distant fast radio burst known so far. The signal came from a time when the universe was only about three billion years old.","The host was surprisingly small. Instead of a large galaxy, the team found a dwarf galaxy that was actively making stars. Its young population matters because different explanations for radio bursts require different amounts of time.","One possibility involves two neutron stars joining together after a long wait. Another involves a young neutron star with an extremely strong magnetic field. The findings make the second explanation more plausible in this case. However, the researchers have not established what causes every fast radio burst."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"burst","phonetic":"","meaning":"爆发；此处指短暂的信号"},{"word":"host","phonetic":"","meaning":"宿主星系；此处指射电暴所在的星系"},{"word":"plausible","phonetic":"","meaning":"合理可信的"},{"word":"established","phonetic":"","meaning":"证实"}],"questions":[{"options":["A small host","A large host with few young stars","A host in which stars had stopped forming","A host matching the expected large galaxy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段以 Instead of a large galaxy 作对比：实际发现的是仍在形成恒星的小型宿主星系。","prompt":"What surprised researchers?","evidence":"The host was surprisingly small. Instead of a large galaxy, the team found a dwarf galaxy that was actively making stars."},{"options":["A pair of old neutron stars merging after a long wait","A young magnetic neutron star","A large galaxy without recent star formation","An explanation proved to apply to every radio burst"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第三段更支持年轻强磁场中子星的解释，但限定于这个案例；并未确定每一次快速射电暴的成因。","prompt":"Which idea gained support?","evidence":"Another involves a young neutron star with an extremely strong magnetic field. The findings make the second explanation more plausible in this case."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/webb-measures-distance-to-farthest-fast-radio-burst-suggesting-origin/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Science","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Its young population matters because different explanations for radio bursts require different amounts of time.","translation":"其年轻的恒星群体很重要，因为对射电暴的不同解释需要不同长短的时间。","analysis":"because 引导原因状语从句；different amounts of time 表示不同的时间长度。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":132,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"A brief radio signal has given astronomers a new way to investigate the early universe. Using the Webb telescope, researchers identified the galaxy behind the most distant fast radio burst known so far. The signal came from a time when the universe was only about three billion years old."},{"id":"nasa-lisa-test-telescope-20261008","title":"NASA Advances LISA Mission Contributions With New Test Telescope","titleZh":"NASA以新测试望远镜推进LISA任务","source":"NASA Science","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/lisa/nasa-advances-lisa-mission-contributions-with-new-test-telescope/","publishedAt":"2026-10-08","topic":"科学与科技","learningReason":"借助望远镜研发报道学习工程流程和未来计划的表达。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 08, 2026","paragraphs":["NASA is preparing a new test telescope for LISA, a future space mission that will study gravitational waves. These waves are tiny disturbances in space and time. The European Space Agency leads the project, with NASA supplying important equipment and scientific support.","LISA will use three spacecraft arranged in a huge triangle. Lasers will travel between them, allowing instruments to measure extremely small changes in distance. Those changes can reveal gravitational waves passing through the formation. The mission is planned for the middle of the 2030s.","The new telescope is an engineering test model rather than equipment ready for launch. It will use a special glass material that resists changes in shape across different temperatures. Lessons from an earlier prototype will help engineers prepare the final design. The work brings the project closer to building instruments for flight."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"disturbances","phonetic":"","meaning":"扰动"},{"word":"formation","phonetic":"","meaning":"编队"},{"word":"prototype","phonetic":"","meaning":"原型"},{"word":"instruments","phonetic":"","meaning":"仪器"}],"questions":[{"options":["Two","Three","Four","Five"],"answer":1,"explanation":"三个航天器组成三角形。","prompt":"How many spacecraft will LISA use?","evidence":"LISA will use three spacecraft arranged in a huge triangle."},{"options":["Its ability to replace the lasers","Its readiness to fly without testing","Stable shape","Its ability to shorten the spacecraft distances"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第三段说明特殊玻璃材料在不同温度下抵抗形变；这是稳定形状的优势，不表示可以跳过测试。","prompt":"Why use special glass?","evidence":"It will use a special glass material that resists changes in shape across different temperatures."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/lisa/nasa-advances-lisa-mission-contributions-with-new-test-telescope/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Science","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Those changes can reveal gravitational waves passing through the formation.","translation":"这些变化可以揭示经过编队的引力波。","analysis":"can 表示能力；passing through the formation 是现在分词短语，修饰 gravitational waves。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":138,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"NASA is preparing a new test telescope for LISA, a future space mission that will study gravitational waves. These waves are tiny disturbances in space and time. The European Space Agency leads the project, with NASA supplying important equipment and scientific support."},{"id":"nasa-arctic-ice-minimum-20261007","title":"Arctic Sea Ice Shrinks to Its 2026 Minimum","titleZh":"北极海冰缩至2026年最小范围","source":"NASA Earth Observatory","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/arctic-sea-ice-shrinks-to-its-2026-minimum/","publishedAt":"2026-10-07","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"适合练习描述年度变化、数据比较和长期趋势的句型。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 07, 2026","paragraphs":["Arctic sea ice reached its smallest area of the year on September 12, 2026. NASA and the National Snow and Ice Data Center estimated that it covered about 4.6 million square kilometers. Several other years share this position as the tenth lowest minimum in the satellite record.","Sea ice changes with the seasons. It usually expands through the cold winter and reaches its largest area in March. During summer, part of that frozen cover melts. September normally brings the smallest area before growth begins again.","The yearly cycle is natural, but satellite observations reveal a longer trend too. The ice covers less ocean at both seasonal extremes than it did decades ago. Comparing many years helps scientists separate one season's conditions from changes that develop over a much longer period of time."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"minimum","phonetic":"","meaning":"最小值"},{"word":"expands","phonetic":"","meaning":"扩大"},{"word":"extremes","phonetic":"","meaning":"极端值"},{"word":"trend","phonetic":"","meaning":"趋势"}],"questions":[{"options":["March","July","September","December"],"answer":2,"explanation":"文章说明最小范围出现在九月。","prompt":"When was the minimum reached?","evidence":"Arctic sea ice reached its smallest area of the year on September 12, 2026."},{"options":["One storm","Many years","One summer image","The most recent winter alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第三段说明跨多年比较帮助区分一个季节的状况与长期变化；单次风暴或一张影像不足以作这种比较。","prompt":"What reveals the long trend?","evidence":"Comparing many years helps scientists separate one season's conditions from changes that develop over a much longer period of time."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/arctic-sea-ice-shrinks-to-its-2026-minimum/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Earth Observatory","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"During summer, part of that frozen cover melts.","translation":"在夏季，那层冰冻覆盖物的一部分会融化。","analysis":"During summer 作时间状语；part of that frozen cover 作主语。这里 cover 指不可数的冰层覆盖，part of 表示其中一部分，因此谓语用单数 melts；不能据此认为所有 part of 结构都用单数。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":132,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Arctic sea ice reached its smallest area of the year on September 12, 2026. NASA and the National Snow and Ice Data Center estimated that it covered about 4.6 million square kilometers. Several other years share this position as the tenth lowest minimum in the satellite record."},{"id":"unesco-youth-world-heritage-20261006","title":"Connecting youth, education and World Heritage for sustainable development","titleZh":"连接青年、教育与世界遗产，推动可持续发展","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/connecting-youth-education-and-world-heritage-sustainable-development","publishedAt":"2026-10-06","topic":"文化与教育","learningReason":"学习文化遗产保护和青年参与的词汇，同时练习概括共同宣言的主张。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"6 October 2026","paragraphs":["Young professionals from different countries met in the Republic of Korea to discuss the future of World Heritage. Their forum took place in Seoul and Busan in July 2026. It connected heritage protection with education, community involvement and the role of young people.","Participants developed a shared declaration. They called for stronger ways to involve young people in decisions and for closer cooperation with local and Indigenous communities. They also asked for investment in heritage education and continued support for projects led by young people.","The discussion treated education and heritage as closely connected. Learning can help people care for important places and traditions. Heritage can also help people understand one another. Participants explored cooperation across generations and the responsible use of digital tools. The forum offered opportunities to exchange ideas and build partnerships around challenges facing the world's shared heritage."],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"heritage","phonetic":"","meaning":"遗产"},{"word":"declaration","phonetic":"","meaning":"共同宣言"},{"word":"Indigenous","phonetic":"","meaning":"原住民的"},{"word":"generations","phonetic":"","meaning":"世代"}],"questions":[{"options":["Republic of Korea","Brazil","Norway","Kenya"],"answer":0,"explanation":"论坛在韩国首尔和釜山举行。","prompt":"Where was the forum?","evidence":"Young professionals from different countries met in the Republic of Korea to discuss the future of World Heritage. Their forum took place in Seoul and Busan in July 2026."},{"options":["A final list excluding community proposals","A shared declaration","A rule ending youth-led projects","A plan to replace heritage education"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第二段说与会者形成共同宣言，内容包括青年参与、社区合作、遗产教育和青年项目支持。","prompt":"What did participants develop?","evidence":"Participants developed a shared declaration."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/connecting-youth-education-and-world-heritage-sustainable-development","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"They also asked for investment in heritage education and continued support for projects led by young people.","translation":"他们还呼吁投资遗产教育，并持续支持青年主导的项目。","analysis":"asked for 后接两个并列名词短语；led by young people 是过去分词短语，后置修饰 projects。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":141,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Young professionals from different countries met in the Republic of Korea to discuss the future of World Heritage. Their forum took place in Seoul and Busan in July 2026. It connected heritage protection with education, community involvement and the role of young people."},{"id":"unesco-online-content-south-africa-20261006","title":"UNESCO trains participants in South Africa to counter harmful online content","titleZh":"教科文组织在南非开展应对有害网络内容培训","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-trains-participants-south-africa-counter-harmful-online-content","publishedAt":"2026-10-06","topic":"社会与发展","learningReason":"围绕信息核查与网络安全积累日常讨论实用词汇。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"6 October 2026","paragraphs":["Young people and youth organisations in South Africa have taken part in training on harmful online content. UNESCO supported the workshops through a European Union-funded project. The sessions reached 104 participants in Gauteng and the Western Cape between April and July 2026.","Participants learned to check information, recognise misleading content and respond to hate speech. The programme also covered privacy, online safety and responsible content creation. It encouraged learners to think about their own choices when reading, posting or sharing information on social media.","The training was designed to have an effect beyond the workshop room. Participants developed plans to bring media and information skills into their organisations and community activities. The wider project aims to reduce online harm while protecting freedom of expression and access to information. Its approach combines practical checking skills with responsibility towards other people in digital spaces."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"misleading","phonetic":"","meaning":"误导性的"},{"word":"privacy","phonetic":"","meaning":"隐私"},{"word":"participants","phonetic":"","meaning":"培训参与者"},{"word":"expression","phonetic":"","meaning":"表达"}],"questions":[{"options":["Checking information","Sharing popular claims without checking them","Creating content without considering privacy","Judging accuracy by the number of shares"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段列出核查信息、识别误导内容和负责任的创作；流行程度不能代替核查。","prompt":"What did participants practise?","evidence":"Participants learned to check information, recognise misleading content and respond to hate speech."},{"options":["Only inside the workshop room","Only among the trainers","Only within private individual study","Communities"],"answer":3,"explanation":"第三段说明参与者计划把媒体与信息技能融入组织工作及社区活动，让影响超出培训课堂。","prompt":"Where should learning spread?","evidence":"Participants developed plans to bring media and information skills into their organisations and community activities."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-trains-participants-south-africa-counter-harmful-online-content","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"It encouraged learners to think about their own choices when reading, posting or sharing information on social media.","translation":"培训鼓励学习者思考自己在社交媒体上阅读、发布或分享信息时所作的选择。","analysis":"encourage somebody to do something 表示鼓励某人做某事；when reading, posting or sharing 是省略式时间状语，说明学习者使用社交媒体时的情境。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":142,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Young people and youth organisations in South Africa have taken part in training on harmful online content. UNESCO supported the workshops through a European Union-funded project. The sessions reached 104 participants in Gauteng and the Western Cape between April and July 2026."},{"id":"nasa-webb-stellar-jets-20261006","title":"NASA’s Webb Captures Commotion From Nebula’s Stellar Jets","titleZh":"韦布捕捉星云中恒星喷流的动态","source":"NASA Science","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/nasas-webb-captures-commotion-from-nebulas-stellar-jets/","publishedAt":"2026-10-06","topic":"科学与科技","learningReason":"通过恒星诞生的报道积累空间位置和动态过程的词汇。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 06, 2026","paragraphs":["Webb has revealed young stars hidden inside NGC 7129, a cloud of gas and dust about 3,300 light-years away. The new view helps researchers examine a place where stars are still developing. Many telescopes cannot clearly observe these stars because dust blocks their view.","Webb detects infrared light with great sensitivity. This allows it to look through dusty regions and reveal more of the activity inside. The stars are at different stages of growth, with the more massive ones developing faster.","A bright central star has strongly affected its surroundings. Material flowing away from it has opened a cavity in the nearby cloud. Its light and these flows also make gas glow. While some gas moves away, other gas becomes compressed. That pressure can create conditions in which additional stars begin to form."],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"infrared","phonetic":"","meaning":"红外的"},{"word":"sensitivity","phonetic":"","meaning":"灵敏度"},{"word":"cavity","phonetic":"","meaning":"空腔"},{"word":"compressed","phonetic":"","meaning":"被压缩的"}],"questions":[{"options":["Removing dust from the cloud","Observing only mature stars outside the cloud","Infrared light","Increasing the young stars’ growth rate"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二段指出韦布的红外灵敏度可帮助观察尘埃内部；它并不移除尘埃或加速恒星成长。","prompt":"What helps Webb observe hidden stars?","evidence":"Webb detects infrared light with great sensitivity. This allows it to look through dusty regions and reveal more of the activity inside."},{"options":["New stars","The immediate removal of all nearby gas","The end of all stellar development","Lower gas density throughout the cloud"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第三段说明部分气体受到压缩，压力可创造更多恒星开始形成的条件；不是立即形成成熟恒星。","prompt":"Compression may encourage what?","evidence":"That pressure can create conditions in which additional stars begin to form."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/nasas-webb-captures-commotion-from-nebulas-stellar-jets/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Science","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"The stars are at different stages of growth, with the more massive ones developing faster.","translation":"这些恒星处于不同的成长阶段，其中质量较大的恒星发展得更快。","analysis":"with 加宾语 ones 和现在分词 developing 构成补充说明；ones 替代前文的 stars。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":133,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Webb has revealed young stars hidden inside NGC 7129, a cloud of gas and dust about 3,300 light-years away. The new view helps researchers examine a place where stars are still developing. Many telescopes cannot clearly observe these stars because dust blocks their view."},{"id":"nasa-rupert-bay-20261006","title":"The Beaver Brown Waters of Rupert Bay","titleZh":"鲁珀特湾呈现海狸棕色的水域","source":"NASA Earth Observatory","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/the-beaver-brown-waters-of-rupert-bay/","publishedAt":"2026-10-06","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"从河流颜色的成因入手学习自然描写和因果连接词。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 06, 2026","paragraphs":["Water entering Rupert Bay in Canada can look brown rather than blue. A NASA report describes the colors seen in late September 2026, when rivers carried water into Rupert Bay and nearby Hannah Bay. Both are at the southern end of James Bay.","The color has a natural explanation. Rivers pass through forests and wet ground, collecting material released by old leaves, roots, bark, and soil. Some of this material dissolves in the water. It absorbs certain kinds of light, helping the water appear brown to an observer.","Tea offers a familiar comparison: substances from plant material can change the color of water. Suspended sediment also mixes with the bay waters. The scene shows how a river connects the land it crosses with the larger body of water where its journey ends."],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"dissolves","phonetic":"","meaning":"溶解"},{"word":"absorbs","phonetic":"","meaning":"吸收"},{"word":"sediment","phonetic":"","meaning":"沉积物"},{"word":"observer","phonetic":"","meaning":"观察者"}],"questions":[{"options":["Plant material","Reflections from a clear blue sky alone","A lack of dissolved substances","The complete absence of sediment"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段说明植物来源的物质溶于水，吸收部分光并影响水色；第三段补充水中也混有悬浮泥沙。","prompt":"What contributes to the color?","evidence":"Rivers pass through forests and wet ground, collecting material released by old leaves, roots, bark, and soil. Some of this material dissolves in the water. It absorbs certain kinds of light, helping the water appear brown to an observer."},{"options":["Heating clean water until it evaporates","Tea","Freezing water into clear ice","Separating sediment without dissolving anything"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第三段用茶水类比植物中的物质改变水的颜色，未说河水需要加热才能变色。","prompt":"Which comparison is used?","evidence":"Tea offers a familiar comparison: substances from plant material can change the color of water."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/the-beaver-brown-waters-of-rupert-bay/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Earth Observatory","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"It absorbs certain kinds of light, helping the water appear brown to an observer.","translation":"它吸收某些类型的光，使观察者眼中的水呈现棕色。","analysis":"helping 引导现在分词短语，补充说明结果；help 后的 appear 为省略 to 的动词不定式。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":132,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Water entering Rupert Bay in Canada can look brown rather than blue. A NASA report describes the colors seen in late September 2026, when rivers carried water into Rupert Bay and nearby Hannah Bay. Both are at the southern end of James Bay."},{"id":"unesco-teacher-shortage-20261005","title":"New UNESCO data: For every two teachers, the world needs one more","titleZh":"教科文组织新数据：全球每两名现有教师还需补充一名","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/new-unesco-data-every-two-teachers-world-needs-one-more","publishedAt":"2026-10-05","topic":"文化与教育","learningReason":"用教师供需数据练习英文比例、数字与趋势表达。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"5 October 2026","paragraphs":["The world needs many more teachers, according to new UNESCO data published for World Teachers' Day. There are currently 107 million teachers, but another 50 million are needed by 2030. This would help provide access to education from the earliest school years through secondary school.","The figures are not only about creating new teaching positions. Many teachers will be needed to replace people who leave the profession. UNESCO reports that replacements account for more than half of the additional teachers required. This makes keeping experienced teachers an important part of the challenge.","The new information also examines how teachers are supported, paid and valued. Ministers, teachers and education specialists gathered in Paris to discuss the profession. The central issue reaches beyond head counts: learners need teachers who are prepared for their work and receive support to continue doing it well."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"profession","phonetic":"","meaning":"教师职业"},{"word":"replace","phonetic":"","meaning":"接替"},{"word":"secondary","phonetic":"","meaning":"中等教育的"},{"word":"valued","phonetic":"","meaning":"受到重视的"}],"questions":[{"options":["All teaching positions are being closed","Only new positions are counted","Teachers leave","Teacher preparation has become unnecessary"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二段明确说需要接替离开教师职业的人；这与新设岗位是不同的需求。","prompt":"Why are replacements needed?","evidence":"Many teachers will be needed to replace people who leave the profession."},{"options":["Preparation and support","Head counts without attention to working conditions","Recruitment without retaining experienced staff","Focusing on new positions alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"末段强调教师需要为工作做好准备并获得持续支持，第二段也指出留住有经验教师的重要性。","prompt":"What supports good teaching?","evidence":"The central issue reaches beyond head counts: learners need teachers who are prepared for their work and receive support to continue doing it well."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/new-unesco-data-every-two-teachers-world-needs-one-more","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"This makes keeping experienced teachers an important part of the challenge.","translation":"这使留住有经验的教师成为应对这一挑战的重要一环。","analysis":"make 使用“宾语＋宾语补足语”结构；keeping experienced teachers 是动名词短语作宾语。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":140,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"The world needs many more teachers, according to new UNESCO data published for World Teachers' Day. There are currently 107 million teachers, but another 50 million are needed by 2030. This would help provide access to education from the earliest school years through secondary school."},{"id":"nasa-wildfire-clouds-20261002","title":"NASA Campaign Explores Clouds Spawned by Wildfires","titleZh":"NASA研究野火产生的云团","source":"NASA Science","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/natural-disasters/wildfires/nasa-campaign-explores-clouds-spawned-by-wildfires/","publishedAt":"2026-10-02","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"从实地研究故事中练习天气词汇、过去时和过程说明。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 02, 2026","paragraphs":["Wildfires can do more than burn vegetation. Under certain conditions, they produce enormous clouds that create their own dangerous weather. NASA researchers studied these fire-driven clouds during a summer campaign across western North America, looking for opportunities to observe them from aircraft.","The clouds can bring rain and lightning, while powerful winds may make the fire below more intense. Some carry smoke far above ordinary weather systems, reaching the stratosphere. Once there, smoke can travel across continents and remain in the atmosphere much longer than smoke closer to the ground.","Finding these events is difficult because they do not always develop when researchers expect them. A fire in eastern Idaho unexpectedly produced a major smoke pulse during the campaign. Such observations help scientists connect wildfire behavior with processes taking place high above the flames."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"vegetation","phonetic":"","meaning":"植被"},{"word":"stratosphere","phonetic":"","meaning":"平流层"},{"word":"pulse","phonetic":"","meaning":"短时间的强烈释放"},{"word":"intense","phonetic":"","meaning":"强烈的"}],"questions":[{"options":["Ordinary weather with no fire below","Wildfires","Satellite observations of smoke","Aircraft flying through existing clouds"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第一段说明这些是野火在特定条件下产生的云；飞机和卫星用于观测，并非成因。","prompt":"What creates these clouds?","evidence":"Wildfires can do more than burn vegetation. Under certain conditions, they produce enormous clouds that create their own dangerous weather. NASA researchers studied these fire-driven clouds during a summer campaign across western North America, looking for opportunities to observe them from aircraft."},{"options":["Close to the ground","Below ordinary weather systems","Stratosphere","Only within the burning vegetation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二段说明烟雾到达平流层后可跨大陆传播，并比靠近地面的烟雾停留更久。","prompt":"Where can smoke persist longer?","evidence":"Some carry smoke far above ordinary weather systems, reaching the stratosphere. Once there, smoke can travel across continents and remain in the atmosphere much longer than smoke closer to the ground."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/natural-disasters/wildfires/nasa-campaign-explores-clouds-spawned-by-wildfires/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Science","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Finding these events is difficult because they do not always develop when researchers expect them.","translation":"发现这些现象很困难，因为它们并不总在研究人员预期的时候发生。","analysis":"Finding these events 是动名词短语作主语；because 引导原因，when 引导时间状语从句。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":134,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Wildfires can do more than burn vegetation. Under certain conditions, they produce enormous clouds that create their own dangerous weather. NASA researchers studied these fire-driven clouds during a summer campaign across western North America, looking for opportunities to observe them from aircraft."},{"id":"nasa-gandak-river-20261002","title":"Rains Swamp the Gandak River","titleZh":"暴雨引发甘达克河洪水","source":"NASA Earth Observatory","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/rains-swamp-the-gandak-river/","publishedAt":"2026-10-02","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"适合学习降雨、河流水位与洪灾影响的新闻用语。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 02, 2026","paragraphs":["Heavy rain in late September caused serious flooding along the Gandak River in Nepal and India. Storms brought repeated downpours to mountainous parts of Nepal between September 24 and 27. Water rushed into the river system, and landslides added to the damage across affected areas.","In some places, floodwater crossed or broke through protective embankments. Fields and settlements along the river went underwater. The river is also known as the Narayani, and water levels reached records at several measuring stations.","NASA satellite observations show how much the river changed. Images from September 20 and September 29 provide views before and during the flood. They combine visible and infrared light to make water easier to identify. In these processed images, floodwater looks blue while vegetation appears bright green, helping observers distinguish flooded land from nearby fields."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"downpours","phonetic":"","meaning":"暴雨"},{"word":"embankments","phonetic":"","meaning":"堤岸"},{"word":"settlements","phonetic":"","meaning":"居民点"},{"word":"distinguish","phonetic":"","meaning":"区分"}],"questions":[{"options":["Heavy rain","Dry weather reducing river flow","Satellite imaging of vegetation","Embankments preventing all runoff"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第一段说明接连暴雨使水涌入河流；第二段写到洪水漫过或冲破堤岸。卫星影像只是观测工具。","prompt":"What triggered the flooding?","evidence":"Heavy rain in late September caused serious flooding along the Gandak River in Nepal and India. Storms brought repeated downpours to mountainous parts of Nepal between September 24 and 27."},{"options":["Vegetation","Roads","Floodwater","Buildings"],"answer":2,"explanation":"文中说明洪水在处理后的影像中显示为蓝色。","prompt":"What appears blue in processed images?","evidence":"In these processed images, floodwater looks blue while vegetation appears bright green, helping observers distinguish flooded land from nearby fields."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/rains-swamp-the-gandak-river/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Earth Observatory","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"They combine visible and infrared light to make water easier to identify.","translation":"它们结合可见光和红外光，使水体更容易被识别。","analysis":"to make 引导目的状语；make 的宾语是 water，宾语补足语是 easier to identify。to identify 用主动形式表达被动含义，指水体更容易被识别。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":135,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Heavy rain in late September caused serious flooding along the Gandak River in Nepal and India. Storms brought repeated downpours to mountainous parts of Nepal between September 24 and 27. Water rushed into the river system, and landslides added to the damage across affected areas."},{"id":"nasa-webb-planet-collisions-20261001","title":"NASA’s Webb Provides Crash Course on Planet-Shattering Collisions","titleZh":"韦布带来行星剧烈碰撞的新认识","source":"NASA Science","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/nasas-webb-provides-crash-course-on-planet-shattering-collisions/","publishedAt":"2026-10-01","topic":"科学与科技","learningReason":"适合学习解释天文学假说的句型并体会标题中的双关。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 01, 2026","paragraphs":["Astronomers are using Webb to investigate violent collisions around young stars. These systems may offer clues about events that shaped our own solar system. Scientists think a major impact on the young Earth helped produce the material that later formed the Moon.","The new research focuses on unusual disks containing large amounts of warm dust close to their stars. Such environments are called extreme debris disks. They are uncommon in observations, even though theoretical expectations suggest researchers should find more of them.","The team assembled information on 21 disks using Webb observations and older data from the Spitzer telescope. Studying this larger collection helps researchers examine the materials present and the energy involved in collisions. Rather than watching Earth's ancient history directly, astronomers are investigating other systems that may preserve signs of comparable processes happening around distant stars."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"debris","phonetic":"","meaning":"碎片"},{"word":"theoretical","phonetic":"","meaning":"理论上的"},{"word":"assembled","phonetic":"","meaning":"汇集"},{"word":"comparable","phonetic":"","meaning":"可比较的；类似的"}],"questions":[{"options":["Warm dust","Only cold dust far from the stars","The material observed directly on ancient Earth","Disks without collision debris"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段说明这些盘在靠近恒星处含有大量温暖尘埃；不能把它们与远处的冷尘埃混为一谈。","prompt":"What surrounds these young stars?","evidence":"The new research focuses on unusual disks containing large amounts of warm dust close to their stars."},{"options":["12","16","21","41"],"answer":2,"explanation":"研究者汇集了二十一个盘的数据。","prompt":"How many disks were studied?","evidence":"The team assembled information on 21 disks using Webb observations and older data from the Spitzer telescope."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/missions/webb/nasas-webb-provides-crash-course-on-planet-shattering-collisions/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Science","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"These systems may offer clues about events that shaped our own solar system.","translation":"这些系统可能为塑造我们自身太阳系的事件提供线索。","analysis":"may 表示可能性；that shaped our own solar system 是修饰 events 的定语从句。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":138,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Astronomers are using Webb to investigate violent collisions around young stars. These systems may offer clues about events that shaped our own solar system. Scientists think a major impact on the young Earth helped produce the material that later formed the Moon."},{"id":"nasa-saskatchewan-agriculture-20261001","title":"An Agricultural “Island” in the Saskatchewan River Delta","titleZh":"萨斯喀彻温河三角洲中的农业“孤岛”","source":"NASA Earth Observatory","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/an-agricultural-island-in-the-saskatchewan-river-delta/","publishedAt":"2026-10-01","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"借助农田季节变化学习农业词汇和前后对比的表达。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Oct 01, 2026","paragraphs":["Fields near The Pas in Manitoba form an unusual farming area inside a wet river delta. Much of the surrounding landscape contains marshes, lakes, and winding waterways. The farmland stands out because its straight boundaries contrast with these natural shapes.","NASA shared satellite views from July and September 2026. In summer, many fields looked green as crops grew. By autumn, many had turned brown as the area moved into harvest season. The views came from two Landsat satellites and show the same landscape at different times.","Water creates both challenges and opportunities for farmers here. Wet conditions can delay planting, while fertile soil and long summer days support growth. Flood protection remains important. Farming in the valley depends on structures that hold water back and pumps that help control it, allowing fields to remain productive within this wet environment."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"boundaries","phonetic":"","meaning":"边界"},{"word":"harvest","phonetic":"","meaning":"收获"},{"word":"fertile","phonetic":"","meaning":"肥沃的"},{"word":"productive","phonetic":"","meaning":"具有生产力的"}],"questions":[{"options":["The geographical location of the delta","Field colors","The names of the surrounding rivers","The town’s location relative to the fields"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第二段对比同一片地貌的两个时点：夏季许多田地为绿色，秋季收获时变为棕色。","prompt":"What changed between satellite views?","evidence":"In summer, many fields looked green as crops grew. By autumn, many had turned brown as the area moved into harvest season."},{"options":["Long summer days","Wet conditions that delay planting","Removing all flood-protection structures","Short daylight hours throughout summer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第三段指出肥沃土壤与漫长夏季白昼支持作物生长；湿地条件也会推迟播种，需要防洪和水泵。","prompt":"What supports crop growth?","evidence":"Wet conditions can delay planting, while fertile soil and long summer days support growth."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/an-agricultural-island-in-the-saskatchewan-river-delta/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Earth Observatory","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"The farmland stands out because its straight boundaries contrast with these natural shapes.","translation":"农田格外显眼，因为其笔直的边界与这些自然形状形成对比。","analysis":"stand out 表示显眼；because 引导原因状语从句，contrast with 表示与某物形成对比。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":139,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Fields near The Pas in Manitoba form an unusual farming area inside a wet river delta. Much of the surrounding landscape contains marshes, lakes, and winding waterways. The farmland stands out because its straight boundaries contrast with these natural shapes."},{"id":"unesco-jamaica-youth-recovery-20260930","title":"UNESCO and EU Support Youth-Led Recovery in Jamaica","titleZh":"教科文组织与欧盟支持牙买加青年主导的灾后恢复","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-and-eu-support-youth-led-recovery-jamaica","publishedAt":"2026-09-30","topic":"社会与发展","learningReason":"通过学校恢复报道学习援助、合作和社区重建的常用搭配。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"30 September 2026","paragraphs":["A school in Jamaica has received equipment through a recovery project supported by UNESCO and the European Union. The handover took place at Tulloch Primary School in Saint Catherine on September 29, 2026. Young people helped organise the project as part of a wider recovery effort.","The school faced problems with buildings and learning resources that had become worse after Hurricane Melissa. The donated materials included fans, tables and chairs. Tablets were also provided through another organisation. These resources were intended to improve the environment in which children learn and teachers work.","The project formed part of an initiative supporting recovery led by young people. It brought together the school community, youth representatives and international partners. Their cooperation shows one way communities can respond to a crisis: identify practical local needs and work together to make learning spaces stronger and safer."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"handover","phonetic":"","meaning":"物资交接"},{"word":"recovery","phonetic":"","meaning":"灾后恢复"},{"word":"donated","phonetic":"","meaning":"捐赠的"},{"word":"resources","phonetic":"","meaning":"学习资源"}],"questions":[{"options":["Peru","Jamaica","France","India"],"answer":1,"explanation":"受援学校位于牙买加。","prompt":"Where is the school?","evidence":"A school in Jamaica has received equipment through a recovery project supported by UNESCO and the European Union."},{"options":["Materials only for a new international office","Equipment unrelated to learning spaces","Classroom equipment","Resources only for the project organisers"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二段列出的风扇、桌子、椅子和平板电脑用于改善师生学习与工作环境。","prompt":"What was donated?","evidence":"The donated materials included fans, tables and chairs. Tablets were also provided through another organisation."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-and-eu-support-youth-led-recovery-jamaica","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"These resources were intended to improve the environment in which children learn and teachers work.","translation":"这些资源旨在改善儿童学习和教师工作的环境。","analysis":"were intended to 表示预定用途；in which 引导定语从句，修饰 environment，相当于 where。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":141,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"A school in Jamaica has received equipment through a recovery project supported by UNESCO and the European Union. The handover took place at Tulloch Primary School in Saint Catherine on September 29, 2026. Young people helped organise the project as part of a wider recovery effort."},{"id":"nasa-fire-cloud-pileus-20260929","title":"Fire Cloud With a Pileus on Top","titleZh":"火积云上方出现幞状云","source":"NASA Earth Observatory","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/fire-cloud-with-a-pileus-on-top/","publishedAt":"2026-09-29","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"通过罕见云层现象练习形状描写和科学解释中的类比。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Sep 29, 2026","paragraphs":["Scientists studying a Montana wildfire noticed an unusual cloud above it. A thin, smooth cloud appeared over a much larger cloud produced by the fire. The smaller feature is called a pileus cloud, a name connected with the idea of a cap.","NASA aircraft observed the scene during a research flight in August 2026. The fire heated air strongly, making it rise quickly. As that rising air pushed a moist layer above it upward, the moisture cooled and formed the smooth cloud. The process resembles air moving over a mountain.","Researchers know that pileus clouds can indicate strong upward air movement. However, detailed observations of one interacting with a fire cloud are rare. Images using different wavelengths helped the team see both cloud features and conditions on the ground, including areas that were still burning."],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"moist","phonetic":"","meaning":"潮湿的"},{"word":"resembles","phonetic":"","meaning":"类似"},{"word":"wavelengths","phonetic":"","meaning":"波长"},{"word":"interacting","phonetic":"","meaning":"相互作用"}],"questions":[{"options":["Rising hot air","Moist air sinking below the fire","The aircraft lifting the moist layer","Cooling ground drawing the layer downward"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段描述火加热空气使其快速上升，推动上方湿空气层；被抬升的空气冷却成云。","prompt":"What pushed the moist layer upward?","evidence":"The fire heated air strongly, making it rise quickly. As that rising air pushed a moist layer above it upward, the moisture cooled and formed the smooth cloud."},{"options":["A river carrying sediment","A mountain","Air sinking into a valley","Water flowing downhill"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第二段把这一过程类比为空气越过山地；共同点是空气被迫抬升，不是火场一定有山。","prompt":"Which comparison explains the process?","evidence":"The process resembles air moving over a mountain."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/fire-cloud-with-a-pileus-on-top/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Earth Observatory","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"The process resembles air moving over a mountain.","translation":"这一过程类似于空气越过山地。","analysis":"resemble 是及物动词，后面不加 to；moving over a mountain 修饰 air，说明空气的运动。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":135,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Scientists studying a Montana wildfire noticed an unusual cloud above it. A thin, smooth cloud appeared over a much larger cloud produced by the fire. The smaller feature is called a pileus cloud, a name connected with the idea of a cap."},{"id":"nasa-greenland-hidden-valleys-20260928","title":"Uncovering the Valleys Hidden Below Greenland’s Ice","titleZh":"揭开格陵兰冰层下隐藏山谷的面貌","source":"NASA Earth Observatory","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/uncovering-the-valleys-hidden-below-greenlands-ice/","publishedAt":"2026-09-28","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"适合积累地形词汇并学习描述新方法和研究发现的表达。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Sep 28, 2026","paragraphs":["A new mapping method has revealed valleys beneath Greenland's enormous ice sheet. Researchers identified 1,943 valleys, including many that earlier maps had missed. Others stretched much farther inland than previous information had suggested. The findings provide a clearer picture of a landscape hidden from direct view.","The technique examines the surface of the ice rather than looking through it with human eyes. Ice moving across buried hills and valleys develops subtle changes at its surface. Precise satellite measurements of those changes can help researchers work out the shape of the land below.","The buried terrain matters because valleys guide the movement of ice. They can concentrate flowing ice and influence how glaciers develop toward the coast. Better maps may therefore help researchers understand Greenland's past while improving their work on the ice sheet's future."],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"terrain","phonetic":"","meaning":"地形"},{"word":"subtle","phonetic":"","meaning":"细微的"},{"word":"inland","phonetic":"","meaning":"向内陆"},{"word":"concentrate","phonetic":"","meaning":"集中"}],"questions":[{"options":["Ice surface","Only exposed land beside the ice","Visible plants above buried valleys","Coastal water alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段说明卫星精确测量冰面的细微变化，再推断下方地形；属于间接观测。","prompt":"What does the method examine?","evidence":"The technique examines the surface of the ice rather than looking through it with human eyes."},{"options":["They prevent all glaciers from changing","They eliminate the need to study ice movement","They guide ice","They show that the ice surface is completely flat"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第三段说明埋藏山谷能引导并集中冰流，因此更好的地形图有助于理解冰盖。","prompt":"Why do buried valleys matter?","evidence":"The buried terrain matters because valleys guide the movement of ice. They can concentrate flowing ice and influence how glaciers develop toward the coast."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/uncovering-the-valleys-hidden-below-greenlands-ice/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Earth Observatory","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Others stretched much farther inland than previous information had suggested.","translation":"另一些山谷向内陆延伸的距离远超此前资料所提示的范围。","analysis":"much 修饰比较级 farther，表示程度更大；had suggested 为过去完成时，指更早的判断。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":134,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"A new mapping method has revealed valleys beneath Greenland's enormous ice sheet. Researchers identified 1,943 valleys, including many that earlier maps had missed. Others stretched much farther inland than previous information had suggested. The findings provide a clearer picture of a landscape hidden from direct view."},{"id":"nasa-desert-blooms-20260923","title":"Boom Year for Desert Blooms","titleZh":"沙漠野花迎来繁盛之年","source":"NASA Earth Observatory","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/boom-year-for-desert-blooms/","publishedAt":"2026-09-23","topic":"环境与自然","learningReason":"用鲜明的植物与景观描写扩充词汇并练习解释降雨的影响。","contentType":"新闻与科学报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"Sep 23, 2026","paragraphs":["Wildflowers brought unusual color to parts of Western Australia in 2026. After a wet winter, flowers appeared across normally dry land. Some local experts thought the display might be the strongest in nearly twenty years, although that was an assessment rather than a final measurement.","NASA satellite images compared the landscape in late August 2026 with a similar period in 2025. The newer view showed more green. Rain had helped seeds that were resting in the soil begin growing, changing the appearance of the region.","Flowers also appeared around a radio astronomy observatory managed by Australia's science agency, CSIRO. The site normally attracts attention for instruments that study objects in space. This time, life on the ground supplied another reason to look closely. The unusual bloom connected rainfall, plant growth, and a landscape used for scientific observation."],"difficulty":"easy","vocabulary":[{"word":"assessment","phonetic":"","meaning":"判断；评估"},{"word":"bloom","phonetic":"","meaning":"开花；花期盛况"},{"word":"observatory","phonetic":"","meaning":"天文台"},{"word":"instruments","phonetic":"","meaning":"仪器"}],"questions":[{"options":["Rain","The observatory’s instruments","Satellite photography","Drier soil than in the previous year"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第一、二段把多雨冬季与休眠种子的萌发联系起来；天文台和卫星是地点或观察工具，并非供水来源。","prompt":"What helped seeds begin growing?","evidence":"Rain had helped seeds that were resting in the soil begin growing, changing the appearance of the region."},{"options":["More green","Less vegetation after wetter weather","Unchanged colours across the region","A surface dominated by winter snow"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段明确说较新的2026年影像显示更多绿色，比较对象是2025年相近时期。","prompt":"What did the newer view show?","evidence":"The newer view showed more green."}],"sourceUrl":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/boom-year-for-desert-blooms/","author":"本站英文整理 · NASA Earth Observatory","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"The newer view showed more green.","translation":"较新的影像呈现出更多绿色。","analysis":"newer 是形容词比较级，修饰 view；showed 是 show 的过去式，描述过去观测到的情况。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":137,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Wildflowers brought unusual color to parts of Western Australia in 2026. After a wet winter, flowers appeared across normally dry land. Some local experts thought the display might be the strongest in nearly twenty years, although that was an assessment rather than a final measurement."},{"id":"unesco-philippine-heritage-lessons-20260921","title":"Ten lesson plans explore new ways to bring Philippine living heritage into the classroom","titleZh":"十份教案探索将菲律宾活态遗产带入课堂的新方法","source":"UNESCO","url":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/ten-lesson-plans-explore-new-ways-bring-philippine-living-heritage-classroom","publishedAt":"2026-09-21","topic":"文化与教育","learningReason":"从手工艺和课堂实例学习具体名词及举例说明的句式。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"21 September 2026","paragraphs":["Ten lesson plans have been selected in a Philippine competition exploring how living heritage can support classroom learning. Teachers submitted ideas based on knowledge and practices in their own communities. Nearly one hundred eligible applications arrived during the competition's short submission period.","The selected plans connect familiar cultural activities with ordinary school subjects. One uses rice terraces and local knowledge to explore geometry. Another brings traditional shoemaking into lessons on financial mathematics. Other plans draw on food preparation, pottery and embroidery. Students can therefore meet school concepts through activities linked to community life.","The approach does not require schools to add a completely separate subject. Instead, heritage becomes a resource for teaching existing lessons. Selected teachers and schools will receive small grants to test and improve their plans. Their experiences will provide practical examples for connecting classrooms with cultural practitioners and local communities."],"difficulty":"standard","vocabulary":[{"word":"eligible","phonetic":"","meaning":"符合参赛条件的"},{"word":"geometry","phonetic":"","meaning":"几何"},{"word":"embroidery","phonetic":"","meaning":"刺绣"},{"word":"grants","phonetic":"","meaning":"小额资助"}],"questions":[{"options":["Two","Five","Twenty","Ten"],"answer":3,"explanation":"比赛选出了十份教案。","prompt":"How many plans were selected?","evidence":"Ten lesson plans have been selected in a Philippine competition exploring how living heritage can support classroom learning."},{"options":["Teaching existing subjects","Adding a required separate subject","Replacing all classroom concepts with traditions","Using heritage only outside school"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二段以几何和金融数学为例，第三段明确说遗产是教授现有课程的资源，不必另设科目。","prompt":"How is heritage used?","evidence":"The approach does not require schools to add a completely separate subject. Instead, heritage becomes a resource for teaching existing lessons."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/ten-lesson-plans-explore-new-ways-bring-philippine-living-heritage-classroom","author":"本站英文整理 · UNESCO","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Students can therefore meet school concepts through activities linked to community life.","translation":"因此，学生可以通过与社区生活相关的活动接触课堂概念。","analysis":"therefore 表示结果；linked to community life 是过去分词短语，后置修饰 activities。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":143,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"Ten lesson plans have been selected in a Philippine competition exploring how living heritage can support classroom learning. Teachers submitted ideas based on knowledge and practices in their own communities. Nearly one hundred eligible applications arrived during the competition's short submission period."},{"id":"worldbank-private-capital-jobs-20260917","title":"World Bank Group Mobilizes Record Private Capital for Developing Countries, Driving Job Creation","titleZh":"世界银行集团为发展中国家动员创纪录私人资本，推动就业","source":"World Bank","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/09/17/world-bank-group-mobilizes-record-private-capital-for-developing-countries-driving","publishedAt":"2026-09-17","topic":"社会与发展","learningReason":"适合进阶学习者练习金融新闻中的增长比较和就业相关表达。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"September 17, 2026","paragraphs":["The World Bank Group says it mobilised a record amount of private capital for developing economies in its 2026 financial year. The total reached 112 billion dollars, compared with 35 billion four years earlier. The institution links this growth to its effort to create more economic opportunities and jobs.","Private capital is money provided by investors outside the public sector. The group has worked to make investment easier by improving coordination and expanding financial tools. These include guarantees, which can help address risks that discourage investors from supporting projects.","The organisation is focusing on sectors with strong potential to create employment, including infrastructure, agriculture, healthcare, tourism and manufacturing. Its next task is to attract a wider range of investors. The central development question is how financial resources can support growing businesses and turn into useful jobs in the economies receiving them."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"capital","phonetic":"","meaning":"资本"},{"word":"guarantees","phonetic":"","meaning":"担保"},{"word":"infrastructure","phonetic":"","meaning":"基础设施"},{"word":"employment","phonetic":"","meaning":"就业"}],"questions":[{"options":["Public-sector funding alone","Private capital mobilised","The number of investors receiving guarantees","Money invested only in tourism"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第一段说创纪录的是2026财年为发展中经济体动员的私人资本，总额1120亿美元。","prompt":"What reached a record?","evidence":"The World Bank Group says it mobilised a record amount of private capital for developing economies in its 2026 financial year. The total reached 112 billion dollars, compared with 35 billion four years earlier."},{"options":["Reducing the number of growing businesses","Expanding investment without regard to employment","Job creation","Restricting finance to a single sector"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第一段把资本增长与经济机会和就业联系起来，第三段列出有就业潜力的行业。","prompt":"What is a central goal?","evidence":"The institution links this growth to its effort to create more economic opportunities and jobs."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/09/17/world-bank-group-mobilizes-record-private-capital-for-developing-countries-driving","author":"本站英文整理 · World Bank","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"These include guarantees, which can help address risks that discourage investors from supporting projects.","translation":"这些工具包括担保，它可以帮助应对那些阻碍投资者支持项目的风险。","analysis":"which 引导非限制性定语从句；that 引导的限制性定语从句修饰 risks；discourage somebody from doing 表示阻碍某人做某事。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":141,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"The World Bank Group says it mobilised a record amount of private capital for developing economies in its 2026 financial year. The total reached 112 billion dollars, compared with 35 billion four years earlier. The institution links this growth to its effort to create more economic opportunities and jobs."},{"id":"worldbank-digital-payments-20260909","title":"World Bank Group Launches Initiative to Help Local Financial Institutions Expand Digital Payments in Emerging Markets","titleZh":"世界银行集团推出计划，帮助新兴市场金融机构扩大数字支付","source":"World Bank","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/09/10/world-bank-group-launches-initiative-to-help-local-financial-institutions-expand-d","publishedAt":"2026-09-09","topic":"社会与发展","learningReason":"通过数字支付场景学习小企业、消费者和金融服务相关词汇。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":false,"dateEvidence":"September 9, 2026","paragraphs":["The World Bank Group has announced an initiative to expand digital payments in emerging markets. The programme is led by the International Finance Corporation (IFC). It aims to help banks and other financial institutions offer payment services to more consumers and small businesses.","Some institutions face financial requirements that make it difficult to join international payment networks. As a result, many people and businesses still depend on cash. The new initiative will provide guarantees covering part of the risk involved in settling payments. This is intended to make participation easier for more institutions.","The programme also aims to reach groups with limited access to formal financial services, including women entrepreneurs. Wider use of digital payments could help small businesses serve more customers. The institution expects the initiative to increase competition and improve access to payment services, while supporting business growth and employment."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"initiative","phonetic":"","meaning":"新计划"},{"word":"settling","phonetic":"","meaning":"结算"},{"word":"entrepreneurs","phonetic":"","meaning":"创业者"},{"word":"competition","phonetic":"","meaning":"市场竞争"}],"questions":[{"options":["IFC","UNESCO","The European Union","The African Development Bank Group"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第一段明确说该计划由国际金融公司（IFC）牵头，帮助金融机构扩大支付服务。","prompt":"Who leads the initiative?","evidence":"The programme is led by the International Finance Corporation (IFC)."},{"options":["Every risk faced by every small business","The absence of financial institutions","The cost of all consumer purchases","Payment risk"],"answer":3,"explanation":"第二段说明担保覆盖部分支付结算风险，以降低机构参与网络的障碍；不覆盖所有商业风险。","prompt":"What do guarantees address?","evidence":"The new initiative will provide guarantees covering part of the risk involved in settling payments."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/09/10/world-bank-group-launches-initiative-to-help-local-financial-institutions-expand-d","author":"本站英文整理 · World Bank","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"Some institutions face financial requirements that make it difficult to join international payment networks.","translation":"一些机构面临的金融要求使其难以加入国际支付网络。","analysis":"that 引导定语从句修饰 requirements；make it difficult to do 中的 it 是形式宾语，真正的宾语是后面的不定式。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":142,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"The World Bank Group has announced an initiative to expand digital payments in emerging markets. The programme is led by the International Finance Corporation (IFC). It aims to help banks and other financial institutions offer payment services to more consumers and small businesses."},{"id":"worldbank-mission300-electricity-20260616","title":"Under Mission 300, A New Way of Doing Business Connects Over 50 Million People to Electricity Across Africa","titleZh":"“300使命”推动新合作模式，让非洲逾五千万人获得电力","source":"World Bank","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/06/16/under-mission-300-a-new-way-of-doing-business-connects-over-50-million-people-to-electricity-across-africa","publishedAt":"2026-06-16","topic":"社会与发展","learningReason":"借助电力普及报道练习大数字、基础设施和发展目标的表达。","contentType":"新闻报道","isArchive":true,"dateEvidence":"June 16, 2026","paragraphs":["More than 50 million people across Africa have gained access to electricity under Mission 300, according to the World Bank Group. The initiative works with the African Development Bank Group and aims to reach 300 million people by 2030. Its latest results cover forty countries.","The programme supports different parts of electricity systems, from producing power to bringing it to homes and businesses. It also works on policies that can make connections more affordable. Governments, development partners and private investors are encouraged to coordinate their efforts around shared national plans.","Electricity access is important for more than lighting. It can support schools, healthcare, businesses and jobs. The initiative combines financing with reforms designed to attract investment into communities that can be difficult to serve. Its reported progress shows how cooperation and changes in policy can help expand essential services across many countries."],"difficulty":"challenging","vocabulary":[{"word":"access","phonetic":"","meaning":"（获得电力等服务的）机会；使用权"},{"word":"affordable","phonetic":"","meaning":"负担得起的"},{"word":"coordinate","phonetic":"","meaning":"协调"},{"word":"reforms","phonetic":"","meaning":"政策改革"}],"questions":[{"options":["Only services for existing power producers","Electricity","Only lighting equipment sold to schools","Only financing for already connected cities"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第一段介绍新增电力服务覆盖；第三段指出电力还可支持学校、医疗、企业和就业。","prompt":"What service is expanding?","evidence":"More than 50 million people across Africa have gained access to electricity under Mission 300, according to the World Bank Group."},{"options":["Separate plans without shared priorities","Financing without policy coordination","Coordinated efforts","Policy changes without any partners"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二段要求政府、发展伙伴和私人投资者围绕共同国家计划协调；第三段补充融资与改革相结合。","prompt":"What helps implementation?","evidence":"Governments, development partners and private investors are encouraged to coordinate their efforts around shared national plans."}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/06/16/under-mission-300-a-new-way-of-doing-business-connects-over-50-million-people-to-electricity-across-africa","author":"本站英文整理 · World Bank","license":"基于公开报道事实的学习改写，非原文转载；来源见文末","sentence":{"text":"The initiative combines financing with reforms designed to attract investment into communities that can be difficult to serve.","translation":"该计划将融资与改革相结合，以吸引投资进入那些服务覆盖可能较为困难的社区。","analysis":"combine A with B 表示将两者结合；designed to 是过去分词短语修饰 reforms；that 引导定语从句修饰 communities。"},"isNews":true,"track":"news","wordCount":142,"hasPractice":true,"loaded":true,"preview":"More than 50 million people across Africa have gained access to electricity under Mission 300, according to the World Bank Group. The initiative works with the African Development Bank Group and aims to reach 300 million people by 2030. Its latest results cover forty countries."}]};
